Ladybird now renders an object element in a shadow tree as it does
in the document tree. Chrome 158, Firefox 151 and WebKit 26.5
(engine-compare) all show an image object and a document object at
the top of an open shadow root, at 100 by 50 and 300 by 150, both
when the shadow root’s markup is set and when the object is created
by script and appended to it.
